# [[ project_name ]]

- Agents must work on a branch and open a PR (`gh pr create --fill`); never push directly to `main` or use the owner's bypass, even when authenticated as the owner.
[% if not private %]
- The `ci` check must pass for agent-authored work. Only the human owner's own work may use the direct-push exception.
[% else %]
- GitHub Actions is disabled for this private repo; run the checks below locally before opening a PR.
[% endif %]
- Never commit secrets, `.env` files, databases or `.DS_Store` (see `.gitignore`; CI rejects them).
[% if py %]
- Python: use **uv** only (`uv add`, `uv run`). Never pip.
- The version is the git tag; never edit a version field by hand.
[% endif %]
[% if not private %]
- Every CI-verified main push is released automatically with the next stable minor version. Manual stable tags use the same build/publication checks.
- Cargo/npm/OpenAPI fields are scaffold seed versions. Release builds materialize the selected tag version without pushing a version-bump branch. Inspect attached release-manifests.json, package metadata and checksums for the release version/source.
- All supported artifacts must pass before a draft release becomes public. A failed upload remains a draft; retry the source/tag without retagging or changing protections.
[% endif %]
- Before committing, run:

```sh
[% include '_checks.jinja' %]
```
